WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.735
-Chloe Fineman!
-Hi.

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:05.371
-It is so great to see you.
-Ah, good to see you.

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:06.505
-I feel like every time
I see you,

00:00:06.505 --> 00:00:08.374
you're in a glamorous,
gorgeous outfit.

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:09.709
-Yes, we were at the Met Gala.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:10.810
-We were at the Met Gala
together.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.245
And we witnessed Pete Davidson

00:00:13.245 --> 00:00:15.147
going to the bathroom
at the worst time.

00:00:15.147 --> 00:00:17.583
-Yes, right as
a gigantic marching band

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:19.718
was about to leave.

00:00:19.718 --> 00:00:21.487
And he was warned that the band
was soon to perform.

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:23.323
-Yeah, we warned him.

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:26.592
Pete was with us at this table
at this beautiful gala.

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:28.695
They were like,
"The entertainment is starting

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:29.996
in three minutes --" Or, no,
"Next."

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.197
Or, "Everyone, please take
your seats.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:32.398
The entertainment is beginning."
-Yeah.

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:34.834
-And he goes, "I got to
go to the bathroom.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:38.170
I got to go pee." And I go, "Oh,
no, it's a bad idea. Don't.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.173
Just wait for the entertainment
and then after that --"

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:42.542
He's like, "Oh, yeah.
I got to go."

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:43.676
They're like, "The entertainment
is starting."

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:45.044
He goes, "Nah, I'm just gonna
go quick."

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:46.879
I go, "Okay, man."
-Right.

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:48.281
But it's also the Met.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:51.784
So you can't pee quickly 'cause
you're in a large museum.

00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:54.954
It takes you 10 -- it's 10 miles
to every bathroom.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:56.756
-Yeah. So he leaves,

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:58.758
and we immediately go,
"This is a bad idea."

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:01.894
All of a sudden you hear like --
[ Imitating marching band ]

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:03.229
A marching band comes in.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:04.997
8'9" Pete Davidson is, like,

00:01:04.997 --> 00:01:07.200
in the middle of a marching
band, like marching back in.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.102
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:12.805
You're like, "That is so
Pete Davidson right there."

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:15.808
Oh, my gosh.
-Shrugged in a kilt, you know.

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:17.477
Yeah.
-How's everything at "SNL"?

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:19.379
Are you excited?
-Yeah, it's amazing.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:23.816
We're back, and, you know,
it's obviously "pandemy."

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:25.584
-Yeah, of course.
-But light.

00:01:25.584 --> 00:01:28.054
-Okay, good. And you have --
And Owen's ready to go?

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:30.022
-And Owen's ready to go.
-Come on, it's Owen Wilson.

00:01:30.022 --> 00:01:31.291
-It's Owen Wilson.
-It's going to be fantastic.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:34.594
-Lovely guy. Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:38.197
-I know you do amazing
impressions on the show.

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:39.866
I've told you this before,
they're fantastic.

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:42.335
Have people reached out to you
and said, "Hey, I like that"

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:45.037
or "Hey, stop doing that"?
-Oh, constantly.

00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:46.873
-Yeah.
-Constantly.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.841
There's never been
a "stop doing" --

00:01:48.841 --> 00:01:52.111
At the Met Gala in the bathroom,
Julia Garner,

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:55.915
who was amazing on "Ozark," was
like, "Why haven't you done me?"

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.850
Which was nice to be like --

00:01:57.850 --> 00:01:59.585
-It's interesting.
"Why haven't you done me?"

00:01:59.585 --> 00:02:01.120
I don't know
if I've ever gotten that.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.388
-Yeah. "Why haven't you?"

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:03.690
-"How come you haven't
done an impression of me?"

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.023
-"What the heck?"
-Yeah.

00:02:05.023 --> 00:02:06.525
You could probably nail her.
You could do a great --

00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:10.430
-Yeah, I'm working on it.
It's coming.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:11.764
-It's coming?
-Yeah.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:14.867
-I know you got a direct message
from Reese Witherspoon.

00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:17.303
-I did, yes, on a mountaintop.

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:19.639
-Now, was Reese on
a mountaintop or you were?

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:23.876
-No, I'll do these impressions
and then it's sort of this panic

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:26.613
of like,
"Have I humiliated myself?"

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.947
Or like, "Do they think
I'm, like, awful?"

00:02:28.947 --> 00:02:32.251
And then this, like, little blue
check thing will appear

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:34.954
in your Instagram DMs
and it's the celebrity

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.055
that you've done
an impression of,

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:37.790
but you don't know
what it's saying.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.892
And to me it's like a letter
from the president.

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:41.627
You know, it's huge.

00:02:41.627 --> 00:02:43.596
So, I was on the top of
a mountain in Montana.

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:45.298
Don't ask why.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:47.967
In the summer,
a ski mountain at that.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:51.804
Yeah, not skiing,
and I didn't have service,

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.373
and I was with my best friend
and I was like,

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:54.840
"We got to go to the bottom
of the mountain."

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.009
-"I can't live without this."
-Reese! Reese!

00:02:57.009 --> 00:02:59.345
-"The view is all good,
but I need this!"

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:00.746
-Yeah, and she was so nice.

00:03:00.746 --> 00:03:03.216
And then I was like, "Whew!"
-Reese liked it?

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:04.784
-Yeah, then we went back up
the mountain.

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:06.919
-Yes!
See, you go down the mountain.

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:08.220
I would do that
for Reese Witherspoon.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:09.889
Go back down then climb back up
the mountain.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:11.991
-Yeah, there you go.
There you go.

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:14.126
-I know you have a lot of wigs
as well.

00:03:14.126 --> 00:03:15.695
-Mm-hmm.
-We discussed this.

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:17.730
How many wigs do you have
in your home?

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.770
-I think at this point,
as a woman,

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:27.673
I have about [High-pitched
voice] 200 wigs maybe.

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:29.375
-I love how high your voice
just got.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:30.743
Do you really have 200?

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.679
-At least 200 at this point.

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:34.847
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.883
-I heard a story and I don't
know if it's true,

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:40.453
but that Brad Pitt was doing
Dr. Fauci on "SNL."

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:42.321
-Yes.
-And they needed a wig for that

00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:45.091
and they called you
and borrowed a wig from you?

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:48.160
-[ Normal voice ] Yeah, so we
were fresh in the lockdown.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.297
You know, and you couldn't
quite, like, Amazon a wig.

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:53.565
It might not come in time.

00:03:53.565 --> 00:03:57.002
Jeff Bezos wasn't there for you.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.002 --> 00:03:58.537
Jeffrey wasn't available.

00:03:58.537 --> 00:04:03.976
So they -- Tom Brooker was like,
"I hear you've got a stash."

00:04:03.976 --> 00:04:06.078
And it became kind of a drug
deal where I was like,

00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:08.547
"Yes, I do have a Fauci wig."

00:04:08.547 --> 00:04:11.050
And then a man showed up
in, like, a hazmat suit

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:13.552
and I kind of, like,
threw it in a bag.

00:04:13.552 --> 00:04:15.754
I wig-dealed.
-Yeah, you did a wig deal.

00:04:15.754 --> 00:04:17.523
-Yeah, I did a wig deal.

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:20.426
-It ended up on --
Here's Brad Pitt.

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:21.426
-Yeah.

00:04:21.426 --> 00:04:22.528
-There he is right there
wearing --

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:24.096
That's the wig. Not bad.

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:25.665
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you, Chloe.

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:26.899
-Thank you.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:28.034
-Thank you, Chloe Fineman,

00:04:28.034 --> 00:04:30.036
for saving
"Saturday Night Live."

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:31.270
-Thanks.
-You really did.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:33.239
-Yeah, I immediately smelled it
when it came.

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:35.475
I immediately was like --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:37.410
And I wore it.
-"It's the best ever," yeah.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.845
-And I mean, he smells great.

00:04:39.845 --> 00:04:41.147
-Yeah, he does. He's amazing.

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:43.215
Are you up for some
new impressions, a game

00:04:43.215 --> 00:04:44.450
when we come back?
-Absolutely.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.619
-Here we go. We're doing
some cool, new impressions

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:48.120
here with Chloe Fineman!

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.422
Come on back, everybody!

